within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.C_CardiovascularSystem.C02B_AntiadrenergicAgentsGanglionBlocking.C02BB01_Mecamylamine;
model Mecamylamine_AlvarezJimenez2017_PD_adaptive_tracker
  "sigmoid_emax exposure-response sweep — Alvarez-Jimenez_2017 :: Adaptive tracker (Percentage of accuracy of the adaptive tracker test)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 29,      // [-]
    Emax = -0.0027,  // [1; % × 0.01]
    EC50 = 9.72e-05,  // [kg/m3; μg L -1 × 1e-06]
    gamma = 1.58,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 μg L -1 per second
  // imax_as_negative_emax: Imax (Q323) enters SigmoidEmaxSweep as −Emax
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 980, Interval = 1.96),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Mecamylamine_AlvarezJimenez2017_PD_adaptive_tracker</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Alvarez-Jimenez R et al., <i>Journal of psychopharmacology (Oxford, England) 31(2):192–203</i> 2017 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1177/0269881116681417\">doi:10.1177/0269881116681417</a>) — Percentage of accuracy of the adaptive tracker test [%] against mecamylamine μg L -1 — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: sigmoid_emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =         29 -        drug-free response (baseline) (BL, Q324)
  Emax  =       0.27 %        maximal effect term (E max, Q323)
  EC50  =       97.2 μg L -1  exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC 50, Q321)
  gamma =       1.58          Hill coefficient (γ, Q325)</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one μg L -1 of mecamylamine per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 29   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (97.2 μg L -1)  response 29
  exposure -> infinity  response 29</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Alvarez-Jimenez_2017: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Mecamylamine_AlvarezJimenez2017_PD_adaptive_tracker;
